Z||000008||Songman||02-22-2001||11:11 AM||||Hoop,<P>Doug told me that you were buying that car... it is a sweet little ride! It was sitting out front as I pulled up at his shop looking all low and mean. And as much as I love my little Indy, I just wish it had that much power!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Songman||02-22-2001||11:43 AM||||Follow up on my trip...<P>I am in Washington D.C. now but before I left Pittsburgh I was taken to a little shop in town called the Auto Palace. What a dream!<P>Now I was in town visiting some of my investors so they have a good bit of money... Well, when the guy asked me if I would ride to the shop with him and drive his Mercedes back I wasn't expecting much. He did mention that I could see some of his other cars...<P>We went over there in his new Hummer. He has a new one because his teenage son rolled the last one.. How do you roll a Hummer?<P>Anyway, we get to this shop and there are some Porsches sitting out front and behind the show room glass are about 6 different 911 configurations. We go down to a side door that says No Entry. As we walk in they are moving a Countach into place on the floor. And they are driving it, not pushing it! What a rumble! This room is filled with all sorts of Ferraris and other cars. Even a black Elf F1 car is sitting there...<P>We walk into the Porsche showroom and he speaks with the owner. As we come back to the other room, they are now moving a black F355 convertible into place. Beautiful car and this is the one I want, but it is so quiet! I was really shocked. I later asked one of the old Italian mechanics downstairs about it and he says everyone always changes the exhaust.<P>Anyway, we go through a door and downstairs into the actual garage. Across the room I see the car my friend wanted to show me. It is the red Diablo that he bought for his wife last year! It is sitting about 4 feet in the air on a rack while they are searching for the oil leak! Beside it on a stand is the motor of another Diablo. And the mechanic is working on a racing 348. tried to talk to him but I think we both just did a lot of nodding because we couldn't understand the accents.<P>I cold go on and on with the cars I saw while I was there. Racing Cobras, racing Ferraris, NASCAR cars... Did anyone know that there were only two real Cobras ever built with automatics? Bill Cosby has one and the other one is sitting here in this shop. Also he has a twin turbo Cobra that was actually signed by Carrol Shelby.<P>Basically, that was my kind of car place! heheh And hidden in the middle of Pittsburgh PA!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||02-22-2001||11:59 AM||||sounds like a nice car collection!  although, i'm not a big fan of Diablo's and Countach's, I love Ferarri's!!<P>And, F1 cars!<P>as for the SE, I really can't wait to see it in person.  i plan on driving it, when my lease is up on the Jeep, until i decide for certain what new/er vehicle i want.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnnyK||02-22-2001||04:28 PM||||Washington DC?? Dude, take a picture of the Exorcist stairs for me!! Anyone!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||kslish||02-22-2001||06:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>before I left Pittsburgh I was taken to a little shop in town called the Auto Palace. What a dream!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That place is sweet isn't it?  Until I was in it myself one day I never knew it existed either and I live in Pittsburgh!  I guess I need a six figure income or something to know about places like that.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Pittsburgh doesn't appear to be much of a exotic car town until you investigate a little further.  The mechanic that I take my car to (for the stuff I'm unable to do myself) regularly has Lambo Countach's and Ferrari 328's in his shop and he own's a Viper.  His labor rates aren't really that high either, and he does the work right the first time.<P>I wonder if Doug would be willing to let the West Penn Fiero Club take a road trip down to his place.  We're always in need for parts (his GT sail panel windows are on my shopping list after I get the GT painted).<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||007DOUG||02-23-2001||12:50 AM||||Anyone (or any group) is welcome to stop anytime. I enjoy fieros, and fiero people.<P>Though you may be surprised when you get here to find I'm not a huge operation like most think.<P>Just let me know when you're coming.<P>Doug||||reg||14
